diagnosis_text:
A thorough multi-layer investigation of it_lab3 and its network path found no fault, past or present. Phase 1 reachability confirmed 0 % loss across all sampled host pairs. Direct probes on it_lab3 showed its eth0 interface is UP/LOWER_UP with a correctly assigned address (192.168.1.5/24) and a valid default route (via 192.168.1.1). The machine successfully pinged its gateway, its LAN peers (it_lab1, it_lab2), and remote destinations across three separate IP segments (servers at 1.0.0.5, internet at 128.168.0.x, office at 192.168.3.2), all at 0 % loss. The l2_snapshot confirmed no duplicate MACs and no down or missing interfaces on any of the 30 lab devices, including it_lab3. The infra_sweep found no ACL drop rules, no static ARP poisoning, and no addressing divergence. The tc_snapshot showed every interface carries only the default fq_codel qdisc — no bandwidth throttling or corruption shaping. The link counter for eth0 on it_lab3 records zero errors, zero dropped packets, and — critically — zero carrier changes, meaning the physical link has never toggled since lab start. journalctl returns "No entries," confirming no historical network events were logged. No flap, stress, or flood processes were found running on the device. The dhcp_link_history and pressure_sweep were both clean. The reported symptom — complete isolation, unable to reach even the first hop — cannot be reproduced and leaves no mechanism or historical trace. Root cause: the claimed outage is unconfirmed; all evidence is consistent with a continuously healthy device. No corrective action is warranted from the network infrastructure side.
=== END ===